# Written by someone else: fetched by script or kept locally, never distributed. Only this
# project's own work is in the repository. The README.md in each */reference/ folder says
# what each of these is, where it comes from and under what terms; NOTICE records the terms.
model/reference/orm-metamodel/
reverse/tests/scenarios/08-bird-drec-case-study.sql

# Sample and benchmark data, all fetched by script ...
examples/db/
examples/out/
bench/bird/
bench/models/
# ... and the copies and listings of it the runs read: BIRD's questions and gold
# (`bench/pilot/sample.py` rebuilds the sample from the download, and
# `bench/pilot/semantic/definitions.py` the modellers' evidence lists from the sample), the
# seventy-question hand run whose records carry the questions, and each database's DDL, schema
# listing and FORML
# (`bench/pilot/material.py` and `bench/ablation/models.py` regenerate them from the models).
bench/pilot/questions.json
bench/pilot/work/semantic/*/definitions.json
bench/archive/hand-run/california.json
bench/archive/hand-run/toxicology.json
bench/archive/hand-run/results-california.json
bench/archive/hand-run/results-toxicology.json
bench/pilot/material/*.ddl.sql
bench/pilot/material/*.schema.txt
bench/pilot/material/*.schema-sem.txt
bench/pilot/material/*.schema-refs-*.txt
bench/pilot/material/*.forml.md
bench/pilot/material/*.forml-full.md
bench/pilot/material/*.forml-sem.md

# Built fixtures and scratch output
reverse/tests/*.sqlite
reverse/tests/scenarios/*.sqlite
reverse/tests/.work/
.work/

.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Spider 2.0, cloned by hand for the probe (2 GB), plus the 435 MB of local databases it
# does not carry and the models reverse engineered from them. bench/spider2-trial/README.md
# says how to restore both. The trial's scratch directories are made from the clone by
# build.py -- the tasks' questions, DDL and knowledge documents, and a `try` script with
# absolute paths -- so only what was written here, answers.json, is tracked.
bench/spider2/
bench/spider2-models/
bench/spider2-trial/work/*/*/*
!bench/spider2-trial/work/*/*/answers.json

# The pilot's scratch directories. `build.py` makes them from `questions.json` and
# `material/`, and they hold absolute paths, so they are rebuilt rather than shipped. What
# is NOT generated -- what each writer wrote, every query it tried, and the modellers' own
# work -- is tracked, because those are the evidence behind `bench/findings.md`.
bench/pilot/work/*/*/try
bench/pilot/work/*/*/lookup
bench/pilot/work/*/*/questions.json
bench/pilot/work/*/*/candidates.json
bench/pilot/work/*/*/draft.json
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.schema.txt
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.schema-sem.txt
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.schema-refs-*.txt
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.ddl.sql
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.forml.md
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.forml-full.md
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.forml-sem.md
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.forml-abstract.md
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.forml-abstract-card.md
bench/pilot/work/*/*/*.forml-nouniq.md
bench/pilot/work/*/*/conquer-primer.md
*.duckdb

# LiveSQLBench Large-v1: the public release is fetched by bench/livesql/fetch.sh (6.7 MB),
# and work/ is the models built from it. bench/livesql/README.md says how to restore both,
# and how to request the gold, which is not public and must never be committed here. What
# is tracked under work/ is what the writers wrote -- each arm's answers, the sample and
# the cost ledger -- and not the working directories `pilot.py` makes them from, which
# copy the benchmark's questions, knowledge base and DDL.
bench/livesql/data/
bench/livesql/work/*
!bench/livesql/work/pilot*/
bench/livesql/work/pilot*/*/*/*
!bench/livesql/work/pilot*/*/*/answers*.json

# The MCP server's local configuration carries connection strings, and its model cache is
# built from whatever databases those name. `mcp/databases.example.json` is the shape.
mcp/databases.json
mcp/models/

# The MCP arms' client wrappers and server config carry absolute paths; the answers and the
# cost ledger are the evidence and are tracked.
bench/pilot/work/*/*/mcp
bench/pilot/work/mcp/bird.json
# which answers are right, against a gold the benchmark keeps private: score_scale.py
# regenerates it for anyone who has requested the gold
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale/verdicts.json
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale2/verdicts.json
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale3/verdicts.json
# SCALE4.md's metadata is built from the benchmark's rows, column meanings and questions,
# none of which the repository distributes; bench/livesql/profile.py and scale4.py rebuild it.
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/profile/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/values/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/meanings/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/descriptions/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/links/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/describe/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/link/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/verdicts.json
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale4/diagnose/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale/diagnose/
bench/livesql/work/pilot-scale2/diagnose/
